{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558676-v20-dav20-and-older-improving-frenzy-controll-for-instinct-based-charcter","id":1558676,"title":"[V20/DAV20 and older] Improving Frenzy Controll for Instinct based Charcter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-06T03:16:37-08:00","id":1558676,"title":"[V20/DAV20 and older] Improving Frenzy Controll for Instinct based Charcter","content":"Hi are there any Merits, Discipline Powers, Rituals, ect. that improve the chance to &quot;Ride a wave of Frenzy&quot; or to avoid Frenzy in the first place for characters on Road or Path that has the virture of Instinct?<br /> <br /> There several that help you to resits Frenzy (like the Merit Calm Heart) but I can't really think of anything that helps you &quot;riding the wave&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T02:43:45-07:00","id":1558786,"title":"","content":"There's nothing coming in mind, but you could use the W20 rule that allow you to spend willpower to choose your target instead of geting a single action of control like in v20. You could also create a merits that reduce by 2 the difficulty to resist frenzy or allow the vampire to not target his ally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T09:30:14-07:00","id":1558837,"title":"","content":"There's a potentially useful merit in DAV's Players' Guide to the High Clans (if willpower is allowed to be spent on Instinct rolls) - Cathartic Fury (2pt mental merit) - roll Courage (diff. 5) after any frenzy, and gain willpower points equal to successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/699-malleusxxiii","name":"MalleusXXIII","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T13:51:34-07:00","id":1561935,"title":"","content":"I think your best option would be to brew a Merit to reduce Diff, but overall the idea for those characters is to not bother and instead adjust your life around Frenzy, so those Merits would kind of defeat the purpose.<br /> <br /> Which makes Instinct kinda lame as a trait that is just straight up less useful than Self-Control. You can try to make something that directs the Frenzy more to the Path's ideal, deviating from basic kill/feed/run while still being Frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T15:02:27-07:00","id":1561940,"title":"","content":"I think there's maybe certain cases where Instinct might be useful, but it definitely seems like more of a niche option when it isn't just objectively worse. It mostly seems like a good choice for vampires optimized for using Frenzy in combat while reducing the risks that come with letting the Beast off of the leash.<br /> <br /> On that topic, what are the best sources for the mechanics of Riding the Wave? From what I recall of DA/V20, the rules are pretty sparse. Did they go into more detail in previous editions, or has the concept always been a bit underdeveloped? It seems like how useful Instinct is as an alternative to Self-Control depends on how much more control you get over Frenzy in return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T15:19:54-07:00","id":1561943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558676-v20-dav20-and-older-improving-frenzy-controll-for-instinct-based-charcter?p=1561940#post1561940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's maybe certain cases where Instinct might be useful, but it definitely seems like more of a niche option when it isn't just objectively worse. It mostly seems like a good choice for vampires optimized for using Frenzy in combat while reducing the risks that come with letting the Beast off of the leash.<br /> <br /> On that topic, what are the best sources for the mechanics of Riding the Wave? From what I recall of DA/V20, the rules are pretty sparse. Did they go into more detail in previous editions, or has the concept always been a bit underdeveloped? It seems like how useful Instinct is as an alternative to Self-Control depends on how much more control you get over Frenzy in return.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why I say it's straight up worse is that you can Ride the Wave with Self-Control just as easily. Instinct doesn't give you a single advantage in doing so.<br /> <br /> And the mechanics are the same at least for modern VtM in all editions: you get to decide your next action as long as it is appropriate to the Frenzy, which means basically choosing a target or direction. Anything else is up to the ST precisely because it's kinda ambiguous, but sincerely not that much, just too limited.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it isn't even worth the effort to try. Just Frenzy and be done with it.<br /> <br /> Instinct for real is only useful to get the Path in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T15:53:40-07:00","id":1561945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558676-v20-dav20-and-older-improving-frenzy-controll-for-instinct-based-charcter?p=1561943#post1561943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason why I say it's straight up worse is that you can Ride the Wave with Self-Control just as easily. Instinct doesn't give you a single advantage in doing so.<br /> <br /> And the mechanics are the same at least for modern VtM in all editions: you get to decide your next action as long as it is appropriate to the Frenzy, which means basically choosing a target or direction. Anything else is up to the ST precisely because it's kinda ambiguous, but sincerely not that much, just too limited.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it isn't even worth the effort to try. Just Frenzy and be done with it.<br /> <br /> Instinct for real is only useful to get the Path in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I didn't realize you had the option to Ride the Wave with Self-Control. I thought that was *the point* of choosing Instinct over Self-Control.<br /> <br /> And the sick Paths, of course.<br /> *stares longingly at the Path of Metamorphosis*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T11:14:59-07:00","id":1561975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558676-v20-dav20-and-older-improving-frenzy-controll-for-instinct-based-charcter?p=1561945#post1561945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, I didn't realize you had the option to Ride the Wave with Self-Control. I thought that was *the point* of choosing Instinct over Self-Control.<br /> <br /> And the sick Paths, of course.<br /> *stares longingly at the Path of Metamorphosis*</div> </div> </div> </div>V20DA changed this. Or, at least, made a goof. But IIRC, it was raised as errata and the dev said he wanted to leave it in as it was. So in that edition only, you can Ride the Wave with either Virtue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T12:40:15-07:00","id":1561977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558676-v20-dav20-and-older-improving-frenzy-controll-for-instinct-based-charcter?p=1561975#post1561975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20DA changed this. Or, at least, made a goof. But IIRC, it was raised as errata and the dev said he wanted to leave it in as it was. So in that edition only, you can Ride the Wave with either Virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I can see potential arguments for it, at least in that specific context. But I'd still expect Instinct characters to have some kind of advantage, since they are otherwise putting certain constraints on their character without getting anything back for it. A valid roleplaying choice, but maybe not fun if you're always feeling shortchanged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T17:45:20-07:00","id":1561982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558676-v20-dav20-and-older-improving-frenzy-controll-for-instinct-based-charcter?p=1561977#post1561977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. I can see potential arguments for it, at least in that specific context. But I'd still expect Instinct characters to have some kind of advantage, since they are otherwise putting certain constraints on their character without getting anything back for it. A valid roleplaying choice, but maybe not fun if you're always feeling shortchanged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically all other successor games ditched both the Virtues as traits and imposing this block where a character can only do one, and never chose.<br /> <br /> And you're completely right, but the point is that the alternative Virtues weren't designed to be interesting options, they're deliberately punitive. You give up 1 dot to make the change and Conviction does exactly the same thing as Consciousness, while Riding the Wave is the inferior option, period.<br /> <br /> That's why homebrew becomes necessary if you want better options for it. IME few players that choose those Paths care that much, but if you're more attentive there's no going around it. And giving Self-Control characters a choice to hang themselves is usually more worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T23:30:44-07:00","id":1562030,"title":"","content":"I think Riding the Wave can be useful if you would otherwise have low Self-Control, since it allows you to exert control over the frenzy without spending Willpower. For combat-focussed characters, frenzy can also be desirable because you ignore wound penalties, meaning Riding the Wave is a superior option. It's a high-risk option, but a better one than the binary choice of control-but-no frenzy/no control-and-frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T00:28:10-07:00","id":1562032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558676-v20-dav20-and-older-improving-frenzy-controll-for-instinct-based-charcter?p=1562030#post1562030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Riding the Wave can be useful if you would otherwise have low Self-Control, since it allows you to exert control over the frenzy without spending Willpower. For combat-focussed characters, frenzy can also be desirable because you ignore wound penalties, meaning Riding the Wave is a superior option. It's a high-risk option, but a better one than the binary choice of control-but-no frenzy/no control-and-frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>In V5 it's excellent, as it just requires you to not roll. But when this sliver of control requires you to make the same roll anyway for each action, that's not really worth giving up on Self-Control.<br /> <br /> One houserule I think could help would be to ditch the roll and let the character decide one action per night per dot of Instinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T02:59:06-07:00","id":1562039,"title":"","content":"I checked V20DA, and actually, I remembered it wrong. It doesn't mention Riding the Wave at all; rather, it makes no distinction between Self-Control and Instinct, except to say that those with Instinct tend to &quot;direct that aggression in a more conscious, desired fashion&quot; (p. 357).<br /> <br /> However, the benefit of this is that the character with Instinct can control their frenzy fully, the same as anyone else, but they might not want to. Depending on how much the ST lets you &quot;direct&quot; your frenzy, you might want to accumulate four successes on your Instinct rolls as soon as possible, and then only bother trying to get that last success when you're ready to regain full control.<br /> <br /> Even though it has rules for Riding the Wave, V20 is also fairly vague. It says the player &quot;may sometimes exert a bit of control while so enraged&quot; (p. 315). Of the two, I'd actually say the V20DA system is better, since you won't be rolling every time you want to take an action but only until you reach five successes.<br /> <br /> In V20, a generous ST might take a leaf from V20DA and allow a Cainite who's Riding the Wave to gain full &quot;control&quot; once they hit five successes, so long as they &quot;channel&quot; the Beast rather than suppressing it. It doesn't say successes are cumulative, as they are with Self-Control, but it also doesn't give any further advice on when the frenzy ends (although we can probably assume the &quot;generally a scene&quot; guideline on p. 299 still applies), so it's a reasonable ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Typo 07-22-2026, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T08:22:44-07:00","id":1562046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558676-v20-dav20-and-older-improving-frenzy-controll-for-instinct-based-charcter?p=1562039#post1562039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's a reasonable ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, but still a ruling that makes things less than optimal without ST conscious intervention.<br /> <br /> Especially because it also offers the ruling where the player doesn't even get to play the character during Frenzy, and it goes for both Virtues.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think it's a working comprise: if you chose to Ride the Wave, you Frenzy immediately but otherwise rolls for control as normal. You have no control over your first actions, but with 5 successes you can retake control. I'd even say not immediately, but when you want. That'd make Riding the Wave a more sound strategy, and clearer.<br /> <br /> Keeping them split by Virtue or not is another call, but with this is a less dire one.<br /> <br /> Merits to circumstantially reduce the Diff of Instinct are still a good option, as that affects the ability to ignore minor triggers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T07:01:21-07:00","id":1562124,"title":"","content":"I'd probably allow each successful roll to grant you control for a turn, even before you hit five successes. That differs from Self-Control (where each <i>success</i> grants a turn of control, not each successful roll), but is balanced by the fact you can direct your frenzy somewhat in any case. Five successes would end the frenzy, but as you say, you can defer the end of the frenzy if you prefer.<br /> <br /> Too easy, maybe? I'd have to play it and see. I would also remove the &quot;ST control&quot; thing. The player here to control the character, but the ST can suggest (and veto/overall, as is their prerogative anyway) an alternate course of action where necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}